 ## Background
-The method originates from the CGAL library's Isosurfacing module, specifically the `CGAL::Isosurfacing::marching_cubes` function designed to work with domain objects like `MC_Domain` [S1]. It builds on the classic Marching Cubes algorithm by Lorensen and Cline (1987) [S2] and adapts it for hierarchical data structures. The `MC_Domain` abstraction allows the algorithm to be decoupled from the specific grid implementation, enabling the use of octrees.
